articles.content_en:
Article 1: Where the defendant raises an objection to jurisdiction during the period for submitting its statement of defense, claiming that the people's court seised of the case has violated the provisions on jurisdiction by level and that the case shall be under the jurisdiction of a higher people's court or a lower people's court, the people's court seised of the case shall examine the objection and render a ruling within fifteen days from the date of accepting the objection:
(1) If the objection is unfounded, the objection shall be rejected by ruling;
(2) If the objection is founded, the case shall be transferred by ruling to the people's court that has jurisdiction.
